WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.530
Forty-three percent of Americans

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:05.580
say they're too tired to function.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.550
So, odds are, you're pretty exhausted.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.410
Some mornings, you might even fantasize

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:15.960
about staying in bed...forever.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.140
Hey, look, your wish came true!

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.220
You've got food, a bedpan,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.660
and an endless stream
of podcasts to binge.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.810
Everything you need to never move again.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.260
But it won't be long until you realize

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.083
that you've made a terrible mistake.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.390
People spend lazy Sundays or
sick days in bed all the time

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:42.320
and are no worse for wear,

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.610
but if you don't start moving
again after about 24 hours,

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:49.950
one of the first things
to change is your lungs.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.960
Gravity isn't pulling them down

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.190
into their normal position anymore,

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:57.420
so the lower part of your
lungs will crumple up.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.000
You probably won't feel any
different, but watch out,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.690
because it's harder for mucus

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.310
to pass through those collapsed passages.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:08.200
So it can get trapped,
which can infect your lungs

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.410
and ultimately lead to pneumonia.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.040
That's why doctors tell people on bed rest

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.850
to sit up and cough from time to time.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:20.030
But you're way too
engrossed in those podcasts

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:21.770
to remember to cough.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.800
Within a week, your
problems only get worse.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.490
You see, normally, your muscles and bones

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:30.800
help support your weight under gravity.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.010
But now that you're lying
down, they're out of a job.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:38.410
And as the saying goes, if you
don't use 'em, you lose 'em.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.180
For every week in bed,

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.540
you lose about 1% of your bone density,

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:47.390
making your bones more
brittle and easy to fracture.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:50.190
That's why astronauts,
who often go for months

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:54.130
without gravity, exercise
for at least two hours a day

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.220
and load up on calcium.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:01.080
In that same week, you also
lose 1% of your muscle mass,

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.350
particularly in your
thighs, butt, and shoulders,

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.410
which you're no longer using.

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:09.016
Now, normally, those
muscles would suck sugar

00:02:09.016 --> 00:02:11.763
from your blood for energy to function,

00:02:11.763 --> 00:02:14.110
but after just 10 days of bed rest,

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:16.680
this process slows down.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:17.900
The result?

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.530
All of that unused sugar can
build up in your bloodstream

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:24.000
and lead to Type 2 diabetes.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.620
By week two, you can start
developing nasty ulcers

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.470
called bedsores.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.370
These form when the
bony parts of your body,

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.940
like your hips, tailbone, and ankles,

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:38.140
press against the same spot for too long.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.700
The constant pressure blocks blood flow,

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.541
killing your skin cells.

00:02:42.541 --> 00:02:43.991
And if you're not careful,

00:02:43.991 --> 00:02:47.710
they could even rip through
layers of skin and tissue

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:50.880
and expose your bones and muscles,

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.530
which sounds like the
opposite of relaxing.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:59.250
Meanwhile, those muscles are
wasting away faster than ever.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.810
After just two weeks,

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:05.230
you've lost a whopping
10% of your muscle mass.

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:07.590
And that causes a new problem,

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.480
because the less muscle you have,

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:13.400
the less oxygen, and therefore
blood flow, they need.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.820
So, after a month in bed,

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:19.260
your heart pumps 30% less blood per beat.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.270
And with less oxygen
circulating through your body,

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:24.280
you feel more tired.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:28.040
Even though you've been
resting for a solid month.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.337
And if you don't get up soon, well,

00:03:30.337 --> 00:03:33.880
you're going to have a hard
time ever getting up again.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.620
Because six months, maybe a year in,

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.460
most of your muscles have wasted away.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:43.000
Your bones are too weak and
fragile to bear your weight,

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.590
and your heart isn't strong enough

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:47.360
to do much work anytime soon.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.160
Meanwhile, your brain isn't
a happy camper either.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:56.140
After all, you've been stuck
in the same room for months.

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:59.950
Staring at the same walls,
the same spot on the ceiling,

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:03.640
having the same experiences day after day.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:06.093
Not great for mental
health, to say the least.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.430
A study of pregnant
women found that bed rest

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:12.610
increased their risk of
anxiety and depression,

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:15.200
and some women reported feeling isolated,

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.810
out of control, and imprisoned.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:21.380
So, no, a year of uninterrupted bed rest

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:25.000
is not the relaxing paradise
we'd all dream it'd be.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.250
And this is exactly why doctors
try to get their patients

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:31.460
up and walking as quickly as possible.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:35.360
In the meantime, medical staff
turn people every two hours

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:36.970
to keep bedsores at bay

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:39.840
and encourage them to do exercises in bed

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.410
to get their heart and muscles working.

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.320
So, just keep in mind:

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.650
There's nothing wrong with
a lazy Sunday morning,

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:51.508
as long as you're up and
moving before Monday strikes.

